# @PROJECT_SLUG@

Features implement `contracts` ABCs and return immutable data or declared errors.
Keep business orchestration in features; presentation parses, calls one service
interface and renders. Construct and inject implementations in `src/container`.
Change a generated contract before changing its public implementation signature.

Use one implementation owner per branch/workspace. Workers receive only their
named feature, relevant contracts/tests and a bounded handoff through the
coordinator's scoped export. This instruction file is not filesystem isolation.
Request exact missing paths/symbols instead of reading the whole repository.
The batch feature needs its implementation, batch/auth/data contracts and batch
tests; it must not import concrete authentication or persistence implementations.

Run `python -m pytest` and `python tools/validate_boundaries.py`. The same behavior
tests must pass for real and mock implementations. Independent acceptance of the
exact candidate remains separate from tests, integration and deployment.

This project starts unapproved. `tools/project_admin.py status` is read-only;
review and owner activation are explicit. No paid, provider, publication, merge
or deployment authority is transferred from the template. Branches are permanent.
